.TH KULAN-WELCOME 1 "October 2026" "Kulan OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kulan-welcome \- Kulan OS welcome tour
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kulan-welcome
[\fB\-\-autostart\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kulan-welcome
opens the Kulan OS welcome tour: choose light or dark mode and an accent
color, install popular apps from Flathub in one go (only apps that run on
this computer are offered), and see which security protections are on.
.PP
It opens automatically once per user at first login, and never in the live
session. It can be reopened at any time from the app grid.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-autostart
Exit straight away if the tour has already been shown to this user or if
running in the live session. Used by the login autostart entry.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kulan-welcome/done
Created when the tour is closed; delete it to see the tour at next login.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kulan/kulan.conf
Product name and website shown in the tour.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR flatpak (1),
.BR ufw (8)
